@startuml Itinerary_Modification_Flow
title Itinerary Modification (UC#3) — Analysis View

actor Traveler
participant "Mobile App" as App
participant "Backend\n(Orchestrator)" as Backend
participant "Edit Classifier\n(Groq Llama 3.3 70B)" as Classifier
participant "Preference Reranker\n(Groq Llama 3.3 70B)" as Reranker
participant "Itinerary Modifier\n(Gemini 2.5 Flash)" as Modifier
participant "Database" as DB

== Step 1: Classify the Edit ==

Traveler -> App: Request itinerary change\n(e.g. "add more museums", "remove stop X")
activate App

App -> Backend: Send modification request
activate Backend

Backend -> Classifier: classify_edit(request, itinerary)
activate Classifier

Note right of Classifier
  EditClassifyAgent returns:
  - edit_type: ADD_PLACE | REMOVE | REPLACE
    CHANGE_PREFERENCES | REGENERATE | ADD_CATEGORY ...
  - target_day, target_category
  - confidence, reasoning
end note

Classifier --> Backend: EditClassification
deactivate Classifier

== Step 2: Route to Correct Handler ==

alt Surgical edit (REMOVE, ADD, SWAP, REORDER, CHANGE_HOTEL)
  Backend -> Backend: Route to _handle_surgical_edit()

  Backend -> Modifier: run_itinerary_modifier()\n(delta operations via Gemini)
  activate Modifier

  Note right of Modifier
    Compact context sent to LLM:
    - itinerary summary
    - available places pool
    - user's modification request

    LLM returns a single delta operation:
    REMOVE / SWAP / EXCHANGE / ADD
    ADD_CATEGORY / CHANGE_HOTEL
    REORDER / RE_THEME

    operations.py applies the delta
    deterministically to the itinerary JSON
  end note

  Modifier -> DB: Hybrid search for ADD operations
  activate DB
  DB --> Modifier: Matching places from DB
  deactivate DB

  Modifier --> Backend: Modified itinerary\n(with _modifier_note)
  deactivate Modifier

else Preference shift (CHANGE_BUDGET, CHANGE_PACE, CHANGE_INTERESTS)
  Backend -> Backend: Route to _handle_preference_change()

  Backend -> Reranker: interpret_preference_adjustment()\n(Groq Llama 3.3 70B)
  activate Reranker

  Note right of Reranker
    Receives current preferences + request.
    Returns structured adjustments:
    - interests_add/remove
    - budget_level, pace, travel_style
    - rerank_reason
  end note

  Reranker --> Backend: PreferenceAdjustment dict
  deactivate Reranker

  Backend -> Backend: apply_preference_adjustments()\n→ updated TripProfile

  Backend -> Backend: Re-rank existing candidate places\n(no new retrieval — Mode 1)

  Backend -> Backend: Re-run planner with updated preferences\n(skip retrieval & ranking)

else Full regeneration (new destination, major overhaul)
  Backend -> Backend: Route to _handle_regenerate()

  Backend -> Backend: Clear pipeline state\n→ re-run full LangGraph pipeline
  Note right
    Same flow as PLAN_GENERATION:
    retrieve → rank → plan → optimize → validate
  end note
end

Backend -> Backend: Validate revised itinerary
Backend -> DB: Save updated itinerary
activate DB
DB --> Backend: Itinerary saved
deactivate DB

Backend --> App: Stream updated itinerary
deactivate Backend

App --> Traveler: Display revised itinerary
deactivate App

== Example: Specific Activity Change ==

Traveler -> App: "Replace stop X with a nearby museum"
activate App

App -> Backend: "Replace Al-Azhar Park with a museum"
activate Backend

Backend -> Classifier: classify_edit(...)
Classifier --> Backend: {edit_type: REPLACE_PLACE,\n target_category: museum}

Backend -> Modifier: run_itinerary_modifier(request, pool)
Modifier -> Modifier: SWAP operation:\nremove place_id=X\nadd best matching museum from pool
Modifier --> Backend: Itinerary with Al-Azhar Park → museum X

Backend --> App: Updated itinerary
deactivate Backend

App --> Traveler: "Replaced Al-Azhar Park with\n the Museum of Islamic Art"
deactivate App

@enduml
